# Perf battery run outputs are never committed (Phase 11 D-02); baselines are.
perf/results/
# Runtime ArtifactStore output of examples/external servers — never committed.
# The archive line is the identity re-point of the line above, added at plan
# 23-04: the ten condemned trees moved to `archive/examples/`, the pattern above
# stopped matching, and 17 generated files under
# `archive/examples/external/00-hello-context/.store/` became visibly untracked.
# The archived trees stay RUNNABLE (D-04), so this output keeps being produced.
examples/external/*/.store/
archive/examples/external/*/.store/
# Build output of `mkdocs build` — never committed (D-02 / 14-RESEARCH Pitfall 6);
# `public/` and `openapi.json` are the committed halves.
site/
# Key material and credential files — never committed (CLAUDE.md §2.2, "never
# a secret in the tree"; LOW-04, D-IMPL-372). `FileBackedKeySource` reads
# `*.jwk`; `FileTokenSource` reads a `tokens.json`; PKCS#12 (`*.p12`, `*.pfx`)
# and Java keystores (`*.jks`, `*.keystore`) are the other shapes a deployment
# drops beside a checkout. `.env` is ignored above; `.env.*` covers its
# per-environment variants. `python -m tools.lints --ignored-secrets`
# (`tools/lints/ignored_secrets.py`) refuses this tree if any line goes.
*.pem
*.jwk
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
tokens.json
.env.*
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local state — agent worktrees and machine-local settings.
# Never a secret in the tree (CLAUDE.md §2.2).
.claude/

# Rendered documentation pages — the GENERATOR and the TEMPLATE are committed,
# the output is not. `page/build_page.py` reproduces it from the tree.
examples/*/page/*.html
!examples/*/page/template.html

# Census evidence — the INSTRUMENT is committed, its output is not.
# `tools/estate_census/` is reviewable in the repository (`D-IMPL-358` ruling 8);
# what a run of it produces is not. Two separate reasons, both load-bearing:
# raw evidence that still carried a credential would become permanent in history,
# and a committed run would read as the census's answer long after the estate had
# moved past it. Reproduce with `python -m tools.estate_census`.
census-evidence/
*.census.json
*.census.xml
*.census.log
